hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1628","###
 Narrated to us 'Amr ibn 'Ali, who said: Narrated to us 'Uthman ibn 'Umar, who said: Narrated to us Yunus, on the authority of Az-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah (RA), who said: The call for prayer was made, and the rows were straightened while we were standing. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to us. When he stood in his place of prayer, he remembered that"
"1629","Narrated to us Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani, who said: narrated to us Yahya ibn 'Abbad. And it was also narrated to us by al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, who said: narrated to us 'Affan. And it was also narrated to us by Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, who said: narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun — all of them saying: narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah.

In the narration of al-Dawraqi, he added: ""When he (the Prophet ﷺ) gave the salutation (i.e., finished the prayer), or he said: 'When he completed his prayer,' he said:

'Verily, I am only a human being like you. Indeed, I was in a state of junub (major ritual impurity).'""

**CHAPTER:**"
